`synchronize: true` in `ormconfig.json` creates both indexes on next start.

### What I could not verify

No `node_modules` and no MySQL here, so I did not compile, run, or `EXPLAIN` any of this — it's reasoned from reading the source, not observed. Two specific things worth checking when you run it:

- `@Index(['author', 'created'])` relies on TypeORM 0.2.x resolving the relation property `author` to its join column `authorId`. `IndexMetadata.build()` does handle that case, but confirm the generated DDL is `(authorId, created)` and not an error.
- The single `follows` index assumes `IN (subquery)` gets semi-join optimized. Worth one `EXPLAIN` on a realistic row count.

### Left alone deliberately

`findAll()` has the identical unbounded-`limit` bug — `GET /articles` with no `limit` also returns the whole table. I scoped to the feed as asked; fixing it changes user-visible behavior of the main article list, so say the word and I'll apply the same two helpers there.

Separately, and not a performance issue: `findFeed` never joins `article.author`, so feed responses omit the author object that `findAll` includes. That overlaps the spec-conformance item already in flight in `CURRENT_FOCUS.md`, so I stayed out of it.

If you'd rather I apply the patch directly, I can re-run the writes with the sandbox override — that's the only write path available in this session.
